{"schema_version":1,"snapshot":"2021-12-03","source":{"repository":"matthiaskoenig/pkdb_analysis","path":"tests/data/testdata_concise_false.zip","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/matthiaskoenig/pkdb_analysis/develop/tests/data/testdata_concise_false.zip"},"sid":"PKDB00383","namespace":"pkdb","name":"Wang1985","licence":"closed","access":"public","date":"2020-12-12","creator":"mkoenig","curators":["mkoenig"],"substances":["indocyanine green","caffeine (137X)"],"identifiers":{"source_study_sid":"PKDB00383","pmid":"4079279","pmcid":null,"doi":null,"pkdb_sid":"PKDB00383"},"reference":{"title":"Caffeine elimination: a test of liver function.","date":"1986-02-17","journal":"Klinische Wochenschrift","authors":["T Wang","G Kleber","F Stellaard","G Paumgartner"],"abstract":"Fasting plasma caffeine concentration and various parameters of caffeine elimination from plasma obtained after a standardized oral dose of 140 mg caffeine have been compared in nine patients with liver cirrhosis, eight patients with non-cirrhotic liver disease and ten healthy volunteers with regard to their ability to discriminate between the different groups. Fasting plasma caffeine concentrations were significantly higher in cirrhotics (11.1 +/- 10.5 mumol/l) than in healthy volunteers (1.5 +/- 0.8 mumol/l). The respective values measured in patients with non-cirrhotic liver disease (3.1 +/- 3.1 mumol/l) did not differ significantly from the controls. Plasma disappearance rate and clearance of caffeine were significantly decreased in cirrhotics (0.11 +/- 0.02 h-1; 1.0 +/- 0.3 ml/min per kg) and in patients with non-cirrhotic liver disease (0.18 +/- 0.04 h-1; 2.2 +/- 0.7 ml/min per kg) as compared to healthy volunteers (0.23 +/- 0.04 h-1; 3.1 +/- 0.9 ml/min per kg). Plasma caffeine concentration determined 12 h after administration of the test dosage discriminated best between patients with cirrhosis (5.4 +/- 1.6 mumol/l), patients with non-cirrhotic liver disease (2.0 +/- 1.4 mumol/l) and healthy volunteers (0.8 +/- 0.2 mumol/l). These results, the safety of the test compound and the simplicity of a single caffeine determination in plasma 12 h after a standardized dose of caffeine make this test attractive for evaluation of liver function."},"row_counts":{"groups":49,"individuals":0,"interventions":2,"outputs":57,"timecourses":3,"scatters":0},"entity_counts":{"groups":5,"individuals":0,"interventions":2,"outputs":57,"timecourses":3,"scatters":0},"groups":[{"study_name":"Wang1985","measurement_type":"species","group_count":"27","group_name":"all","max":null,"substance":null,"count":27,"calculation_type":"sample mean","group_parent_pk":null,"sd":null,"unit":null,"se":null,"min":null,"cv":null,"median":null,"group_pk":836,"characteristica_pk":18292,"mean":null,"choice":"homo sapiens","value":null},{"study_name":"Wang1985","measurement_type":"sex","group_count":"27","group_name":"all","max":null,"substance":null,"count":20,"calculation_type":"sample mean","group_parent_pk":null,"sd":null,"unit":null,"se":null,"min":null,"cv":null,"median":null,"group_pk":836,"characteristica_pk":18293,"mean":null,"choice":"M","value":null},{"study_name":"Wang1985","measurement_type":"sex","group_count":"27","group_name":"all","max":null,"substance":null,"count":7,"calculation_type":"sample mean","group_parent_pk":null,"sd":null,"unit":null,"se":null,"min":null,"cv":null,"median":null,"group_pk":836,"characteristica_pk":18294,"mean":null,"choice":"F","value":null},{"study_name":"Wang1985","measurement_type":"overnight fast","group_count":"27","group_name":"all","max":null,"substance":null,"count":27,"calculation_type":"sample mean","group_parent_pk":null,"sd":null,"unit":null,"se":null,"min":null,"cv":null,"median":null,"group_pk":836,"characteristica_pk":18295,"mean":null,"choice":"Y","value":null},{"study_name":"Wang1985","measurement_type":"abstinence","group_count":"27","group_name":"all","max":null,"substance":"caffeine","count":27,"calculation_type":"sample mean","group_p